From: Perseus Platform <platform@perseus.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm/rpi4: accept the BCM2711 PM compatible for reset

The deployed BCM2711 DTB advertises brcm,bcm2711-pm and
brcm,bcm2835-pm-wdt, not brcm,bcm2835-pm. The latter-only lookup
returns NULL and the watchdog reset is never attempted. Match the
BCM2711 PM node as well and keep it out of the hardware domain.

Keep the existing register translation, password and reset sequence.
The old compatible remains supported. Hardware reboot is not tested.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/xen/arch/arm/platforms/brcm-raspberry-pi.c
+++ b/xen/arch/arm/platforms/brcm-raspberry-pi.c
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@
     DT_MATCH_COMPATIBLE("brcm,bcm2835-aux"),
     /* Special device used for rebooting */
     DT_MATCH_COMPATIBLE("brcm,bcm2835-pm"),
+    DT_MATCH_COMPATIBLE("brcm,bcm2711-pm"),
     { /* sentinel */ },
 };
 
@@ -61,6 +62,8 @@
     int ret;
 
     node = dt_find_compatible_node(NULL, NULL, "brcm,bcm2835-pm");
+    if ( !node )
+        node = dt_find_compatible_node(NULL, NULL, "brcm,bcm2711-pm");
     if ( !node )
         return NULL;
 
